ed(), and loadLocalRecords() (parsing the entire semester's JSON history on the main thread).   Impact: Increases cold start time and blocks the initial frame render.   Redundant Double-Pass PDF Layout (PdfReportRenderer.render):Root Cause: PdfReportRenderer.render() executes draw(data, totalPages = 0, sink = null) to count pages—which creates a full PdfDocument, allocates Canvas pages, builds hundreds of StaticLayout instances, and draws them into native memory—and then immediately runs draw(data, totalPages = pages, sink = outFile) a second time.   Impact: Doubles CPU and native memory allocation time during PDF generation.   B. Recomposition & State Bottlenecks (Verified in MainActivity.kt, Models.kt, AttendanceRepository.kt)Unstable Domain Models Breaking Compose Skipping (Models.kt, Milestone.kt, ReportAnalyticsEngine.kt, BunkPlannerModels.kt):Root Cause:StudentProfile contains var isDarkMode: Boolean, var isOnboardingCompleted: Boolean, and val updatedAt: com.google.firebase.Timestamp?. Because var properties and external Timestamp classes are treated as unstable by the Compose compiler, any composable accepting StudentProfile (or derived states containing it) is never skipped during recomposition.   Milestone, DayReport, SubjectReport, ReportAnalytics, BunkOption, and BunkDayEntry contain standard List<T> properties (List<Int>, List<SessionEntry>, List<DayReport>, etc.), which the Compose compiler marks as unstable unless annotated with @Immutable or @Stable.   Impact: Forces full subtree recompositions across HomeScreen, AttendanceScreen, ReportsScreen, and SettingsScreen whenever any unrelated state changes.   Single-Slot Analytics Cache Thrashing (AttendanceRepository.kt):Root Cause: AttendanceRepository stores only a single cachedAnalysis: Pair<CachedAnalysisKey, ReportAnalytics>?. Furthermore, CachedAnalysisKey computes _recordsMap.value.hashCode() and _holidayOverrides.value.hashCode() on every call to getOrComputeAnalytics() (which iterates over every entry in the nested map to compute the hash). Worse, when ReportsScreen or HomeScreen requests analytics for the current month and then compares it with the previous month or archive months (archiveMonths loops over all candidate months), the single cache slot is overwritten on every call, causing $O(N \times \text{days})$ recalculations per frame.   Combinatorial Allocation in BunkPlannerEngine.plan():Root Cause: Generates all contiguous bunk intervals $O(N^2)$ and evaluates each candidate by allocating multiple intermediate lists (c.bunkDays.flatMap { it.manual }, .groupBy { it.subject.code }, .mapValues, .sortedBy). If triggered on the main thread during state updates, it causes GC pauses and UI freezes.   C. Rendering, GPU, and Animation Bottlenecks (Verified in MainActivity.kt & High-Confidence UI Analysis)Full-Screen Haze Blur + Overlapping Translucent Layers + Continuous StarfieldCanvas (MainActivity.kt):Root Cause: In MainActivity.kt, the entire AnimatedContent host is wrapped in .haze(state = hazeState) while StarfieldCanvas renders continuously underneath, and TopEdgeBlur, ProgressiveEdgeBlur, and GlassDock sit on top.   Why It Hurts GPU & Frame Pacing:When StarfieldCanvas animates every frame (60–120 fps) or when a screen transition (AnimatedContent with simultaneous fadeIn + slideInHorizontally + scaleIn + fadeOut + slideOutHorizontally + scaleOut) occurs, Haze must re-capture and re-blur the underlying render node every single frame.   In Light Theme, MainActivity.kt allocates three Brush.radialGradient objects inside the drawBehind lambda on every draw pass, covering nearly the entire screen three times over (radius = size.width * 0.95f, 0.85f, 0.80f)—causing massive 3x full-screen overdraw before a single UI component is drawn.   Release Build Running Without R8/Minification (app/build.gradle.kts):Root Cause: In app/build.gradle.kts, buildTypes.release has isMinifyEnabled = false.   Impact: Jetpack Compose relies heavily on R8 inlining, dead-code elimination, and lambda optimization in release builds. Running Compose with isMinifyEnabled = false leaves debug-level overhead and unoptimized dispatch in production APKs.   Deliverable B: Before-and-After Comparison PlanBecause physical device profiling tools (Perfetto, Android Studio CPU/Memory Profiler) cannot be executed inside this static analysis environment, no baseline numbers are invented. Use the following verification matrix to measure before and after applying the optimizations:MetricCurrent BaselineExpected TargetVerificationFrame stabilityMeasure on device (P50 / P95 / P99 frame time)$< 16.6\text{ ms}$ (60Hz) / $< 8.3\text{ ms}$ (120Hz)Perfetto / System TraceJanky framesMeasure % janky frames during tab switch & attendance tap$< 1\%$ janky frames during navigation & scrollingMacrobenchmark FrameTimingMetric / JankStatsRecompositionMeasure via Layout Inspector recomposition countsZero parent/unrelated recompositions on period tap or starfield tickAndroid Studio Layout InspectorMemory usageMeasure heap allocations during scrolling & PDF buildZero per-frame object allocations in drawBehind / Canvas; 50% fewer StaticLayout allocations in PDFAndroid Studio Memory ProfilerScrollingObserved stuttering in AttendanceScreen & ReportsScreenUninterrupted 60/90/120Hz scrolling across all listsPhysical device testing + GPU Overdraw debugTransitionsObserved jitter during AnimatedContent tab switchesSmooth 380ms directional slide/scale without Haze stallsFrame metrics (adb shell dumpsys gfxinfo)Deliverable C: File-by-File Optimization PlanFiles Requiring Targeted Performance Modificationsapp/src/main/java/com/example/MainActivity.kt (CRITICAL)Function: MainAppContent.   Issues:Recreates three Brush.radialGradient instances inside drawBehind on every draw pass.   AnimatedContent tab transitions run simultaneous scaleIn/scaleOut + slideInHorizontally/slideOutHorizontally + fadeIn/fadeOut inside .haze(state = hazeState), forcing full-screen RenderNode invalidation and blur